cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use paper-scaffold, please cite this software using these metadata."
title: "paper-scaffold: provenance-checked Typst manuscripts that are safe for AI agents to edit"
abstract: >-
  paper-scaffold is a Typst manuscript scaffold in which every number in the
  prose is read by id from a declaration file written by the analysis, with a
  checksum, a record of the code and data behind it, and guards on what the
  prose assumes about it. A static gate reports stale figures, tables and
  builds without re-running the analysis, and checks prose rules, word limits
  and journal profiles. Word export goes through pandoc with native equations.
  An edit guard lets a wording pass drop a number but never invent one, and a
  set of packaged agent skills audits claims and methods against the code that
  computes them.
type: software
